 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new sanitary sewer main, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 7375 Nolensville Road in Williamson County, also known as Nolensville Town Square – Phase 2 (MWS Project No. 26-SL-112 and Proposal No. 2026M-075ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 1,611 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), 14 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 7375 Nolensville Road in Williamson County, also known as Nolensville Town Square – Phase 2, is needed to construct Project No. 26-SL-112; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M075ES-001 on August 17, 2026, for the acceptance of said sanitary sewer main, sanitary sewer manholes, and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 1,611 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), 14 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 7375 Nolensville Road in Williamson County, also known as Nolensville Town Square – Phase 2, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nMap & Parcel: (Williamson)\t\t\t\tAddress:\nTax Map; 059 Parcel 05200\t\t\t\t7375 Nolensville Road\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance accepts approximately 1,611 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), 14 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 7375 Nolensville Road in Williamson County, also known as Nolensville Town Square - Phase 2.\n\nFuture amendments to this legislation may be approved by resolution. This ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated easements have no market value according to the Department of Water and Sewerage Services.\n\n"
}
